                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It´s good. A short little experience (about an hour to 90 minutes max), which seems surreal at first, but in a certain sense becomes very real as you progress. Now I do have to warn you, the game can seem strange and confusing, even some basic familiar things such as an Escape menu are missing, but I am very sure that is exactly the author´s intention for the chosen subject matter. You operate in an unknown world which seems strange, unfamiliar and completely foreign, as our first-country nations would seem to someone coming form other worlds. In my opinion a very good idea with an execution which fits perfectly. But be prepared to be confused, and do not be afraid to explore while playing this.\n\nThe soundtrack and graphics are right up my alley, for me a 10/10 on artistic choices in this game.\n\nI will give you just a small bit of advice: At the very end, click on the mailboxes, that is something that confused me a bit too much.\n\nBut otherwise prepare youself for a very unique and original experience.",
